.TH FUCHSIA-STUDIO 1
.SH NAME
fuchsia-studio \- explain and check Workbench Studio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fuchsia-studio
.RI { help | health | man }
.br
.B health.sh
.br
.B man fuchsia-studio
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B help
Explain visible regions and screen language.
.TP
.B health
Check the Linux CLI and runtime boundary.
.TP
.B man
Print the manual without requiring a pager.
.SH SCREEN LANGUAGE
Workspaces select Build, Research, or Ops context.
The left rail launches apps; highlight means active.
Windows is the visible tile count.
Active view receives keyboard input.
Spacing is the pixel gap between tiles.
WM health reports window-manager render activity.
.SH LIMITS
Linux health does not invent desktop state. Inspect is the authoritative visible desktop diagnostics surface.
